== The Final Forty — Questions

#mcq(1, [Which of these organisms is unicellular and eukaryotic?], [Yeast], [A bacterium], [*Spirogyra*], [A moss plant])

#mcq(2, [Which structure is found in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells?], [Nuclear envelope], [Cell membrane], [Mitochondrion], [Chloroplast])

#mcq(3, [Homologous chromosomes pair up to form bivalents during], [prophase II], [metaphase of mitosis], [telophase I], [prophase I])

#mcq(4, [The main reason a leaf is thin is that], [it must be able to bend], [it reduces the area for light], [carbon dioxide has only a short distance to diffuse to the cells], [it stores more water])

#mcq(5, [The pH in the stomach is about], [7], [2], [9], [11])

#mcq(6, [Water moves from the leaf xylem into the mesophyll cells because], [the xylem is dead], [photosynthesis pushes it], [the mesophyll cells have a lower water potential than the xylem sap], [the cuticle absorbs it])

#mcq(7, [Platelets are important because they], [help to clot blood at a wound], [carry oxygen], [produce antibodies], [transport fat])

#mcq(8, [Insects exchange gases through], [gills], [lungs], [the body surface only], [a system of tracheae opening at spiracles])

#mcq(9, [The concentration of urine is controlled mainly by], [insulin from the pancreas], [ADH (antidiuretic hormone) from the pituitary], [adrenaline from the adrenal gland], [thyroxine from the thyroid])

#mcq(10, [The skeleton of an insect is called an exoskeleton because it is], [made of bone on the inside], [made of cartilage], [fluid-filled], [on the outside of the body and made mainly of chitin])

#mcq(11, [*Euglena* is placed in the kingdom Protista rather than Plantae because it], [has no cellulose cell wall and can feed heterotrophically], [has no chlorophyll], [is multicellular], [lacks a nucleus])

#mcq(12, [The pancreas is an example of], [a tissue], [a single cell], [an organ that is also a gland], [an organ system])

#mcq(13, [Meiosis II is similar to mitosis because in both], [homologous chromosomes pair], [the chromosome number is halved], [crossing over occurs], [sister chromatids separate])

#mcq(14, [The balanced equation for photosynthesis shows that six molecules of carbon dioxide combine with six molecules of water to give], [glucose and six molecules of carbon dioxide], [glucose and six molecules of oxygen], [starch and water], [sucrose and oxygen])

#mcq(15, [Peristalsis is], [the chemical breakdown of food], [the absorption of water], [a wave of muscular contraction that moves food along the gut], [the secretion of bile])

#mcq(16, [The water potential of pure water at atmospheric pressure is], [zero], [one], [negative], [undefined])

#mcq(17, [Valves in the heart and veins ensure that], [blood flows in one direction only], [blood pressure is reduced], [blood is oxygenated], [plasma does not leak out])

#mcq(18, [The main advantage of aerobic over anaerobic respiration is that aerobic respiration], [is faster], [produces alcohol], [needs no enzymes], [releases far more energy per glucose molecule])

#mcq(19, [Osmoregulation is control of the], [body temperature], [blood glucose level], [water and salt balance of the body], [rate of breathing])

#mcq(20, [Plant stems and leaves wilt when they lack water because], [the xylem contracts], [cells lose turgor and cannot hold the plant upright], [the cell walls dissolve], [the roots shrink])

#mcq(21, [Saprophytic nutrition is shown by a fungus that], [engulfs food particles with pseudopodia], [photosynthesises in sunlight], [secretes enzymes onto dead matter and absorbs the soluble products], [absorbs food from a living host without killing it])

#mcq(22, [The folded inner membrane (cristae) of a mitochondrion increases], [the strength of the cell wall], [the surface area for the enzymes of aerobic respiration], [the volume of cell sap], [the rate of photosynthesis])

#mcq(23, [Which pair of events produces genetic variation during meiosis?], [Crossing over and independent assortment], [DNA replication and cytokinesis], [Cell growth and respiration], [Spindle formation and lysis])

#mcq(24, [The products of photosynthesis are transported out of the leaf in the], [xylem], [stomata], [cuticle], [phloem])

#mcq(25, [Bile assists fat digestion by], [hydrolysing fat into fatty acids], [absorbing glycerol], [emulsifying fats into small droplets, increasing the surface for lipase], [making the chyme acidic])

#mcq(26, [Which of these conditions would make transpiration fastest?], [Cold, humid and still], [Cool, humid and windy], [Hot, humid and still], [Hot, dry and windy])

#mcq(27, [The purpose of the pericardium is to], [protect and lubricate the heart], [pump blood], [store glycogen], [make antibodies])

#mcq(28, [In a bony fish, water flows over the gills], [in the same direction as the blood], [in the opposite direction to the blood, maintaining a diffusion gradient], [only when the fish is out of water], [through the mouth only])

#mcq(29, [The sweat glands of the skin lie in the], [dermis], [epidermis], [subcutaneous fat layer], [hair follicle only])

#mcq(30, [The ribs are attached to the sternum by], [ligament only], [tendon only], [cartilage], [muscle])

#mcq(31, [Binomial nomenclature uses names that are], [in English only], [Latinised and understood internationally], [changed with each new textbook], [the same as the common names])

#mcq(32, [Which organelle has no membrane at all?], [Mitochondrion], [Lysosome], [Vacuole], [Ribosome])

#mcq(33, [The chief significance of meiosis is that it], [doubles the chromosome number], [produces identical cells for growth], [repairs damaged tissue], [halves the chromosome number and creates variation])

#mcq(34, [Which of the following would *increase* the rate of photosynthesis in a well-watered plant on a dull day?], [Reducing the light intensity further], [Removing all the leaves], [Increasing the carbon dioxide concentration in the air], [Lowering the temperature to 2 °C])

#mcq(35, [Incisors are adapted for], [grinding food], [cutting and biting food], [tearing flesh], [crushing bone])

#mcq(36, [Water rises in the xylem of a tall tree during the day mainly because], [transpiration at the leaves lowers the pressure at the top of the column], [water is pumped up by the living cells of the root], [the xylem contracts], [active transport moves water])

#mcq(37, [Capillaries are ideally suited for exchange because they], [have thick muscular walls], [are one cell thick with a large total surface area], [contain valves], [carry only deoxygenated blood])

#mcq(38, [A bread dough rises because the yeast in it releases], [oxygen], [nitrogen], [lactic acid], [carbon dioxide])

#mcq(39, [The bladder stores urine until], [stretch receptors in its walls trigger the urge to empty it], [ADH is released], [the kidneys stop working], [digestion is complete])

